        "original_id": "ca8a2eef-e6d9-5c85-bee3-aa0fc22adb28",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sigmund Jähn, Christer Fuglesang, Darin\n- Roles: cosmonaut, pilot, physicist, ESA astronaut\n- Organizations: ESA, Soviet Union\n- Programs and Missions: Interkosmos programme, STS-116 Space Shuttle mission\n- Products: “Breathing Your Love” single\n- Places: Stockholm, space\n\nFacts:\n- Sigmund Jähn was born on 13 February 1937.\n- Sigmund Jähn is a German cosmonaut and pilot.\n- In 1978, Sigmund Jähn became the first East German and the first German native to fly in space as part of the Soviet Union's Interkosmos programme.\n- Christer Fuglesang was born in Stockholm on March 18, 1957.\n- Christer Fuglesang is a Swedish physicist and an ESA astronaut.\n- On December 10, 2006, at 01:47 GMT, Christer Fuglesang launched aboard the STS-116 Space Shuttle mission and became the first Swedish citizen in space.\n- In October 2009, Christer Fuglesang took two copies of Darin's single “Breathing Your Love” into space because his daughter was a Darin fan.\n- A photo of the “Breathing Your Love” disc with Earth in the distance was published on Darin's official website.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
